messages:
maria (Docs): quick flag 1: product wants to flip hosted default from 'redwood-1' to 'redwood-1-rlhf' on 2026-04-18. need a tiny migration doc + scan for snippets in quickstarts/examples. can someone own editing and a follow-up review?
zoe (Eng): I can sweep examples and the runtime docs. i'll run a tokenized grep for "redwood-1" and for old streaming patterns like `client.stream()` and `choices[0].text`.
ben (SDK): Heads-up: v1->v2 SDK diffs we must reflect: `client.generate()` -> `client.responses.create()` and streaming is now an async iterator over event objects. also param nesting changed (no top-level params.*). i'll put a compatibility snippet in the SDK repo and attach to the docs PR.
maria (Docs): good. prefer short migration snippet in docs: show old call -> new call + tiny shim. and a note that alias will be kept for 30 days.
sam (Support): Please include a one-paragraph support blurb we can paste into tickets: customers keep hitting the old quickstart and get runtime errors. also collect any customer snippets to avoid breaking them.
lina (PM): We'll keep the alias redirect for 30 days and send a console banner. docs should recommend explicit model IDs. add rollback steps for Dedicated customers who pin versions.
zoe (Eng): Found 12 occurrences across /docs, /examples, and /sdk-snippets. i'll push a branch with fixes and link files in the PR description.
ben (SDK): Draft compatibility shim (will add to SDK tests): ```js
// v1 shim for a short transition
function generateShim(opts){
  const model = opts.model || 'redwood-1-rlhf';
  return client.responses.create({ model, input: opts.input || opts.prompt });
}
```
This preserves the simplest callsites.
maria (Docs): For the quickstart, let's show the new streaming loop explicitly. e.g. ```ts
const stream = await client.responses.stream({ model: 'redwood-1-rlhf', input: 'hello world' });
for await (const ev of stream) {
  if (ev.type === 'response.delta') process.stdout.write(ev.delta);
}
``` keep it minimal.
ben (SDK): i'll include that exact snippet in the SDK PR so quickstarts can link to a canonical snippet. PR draft: #3505.
sam (Support): Draft blurb: "Default hosted model changed to redwood-1-rlhf. redwood-1 alias deprecated for 30 days. Update SDK usage: use client.responses.create / client.responses.stream. Contact support if you need a Dedicated rollback." i'll paste to #support-ready after kate's edit.
maria (Docs): timeline: docs PRs open by 2026-04-12, merge by 2026-04-16 so preview builds are available (deploy window 2026-04-17). tag me for final proof.
deploy-bot: Reminder: docs preview builds may take ~20m. request previews before 2026-04-17 21:30 UTC.
zoe (Eng): acked. i'll send the file list in the PR and add a changelog line.
maria (Docs): thanks all. last note: add a tiny troubleshooting section: 1) SDK error about missing choices -> point to streaming change 2) temperature location change -> show mapping. that'll cut support noise.
ben (SDK): will add mapping table to migration doc and a test asserting old param aliases still work for 30 days.
maria (Docs): perfect. i'll open the meta PR to wire the redirect rules once your PRs land. ping when green. :rocket:
